      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017. Published by Elsevier Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "CRISPR-Cas-mediated defense against phage invaders usually requires recognition of short sequences, termed protospacer-adjacent motifs (PAMs), in phage DNA. In this issue of Cell Host & Microbe, Pyenson et al. (2017) show that the lack of a PAM requirement in some CRISPR-Cas systems prevents interference evasion and facilitates phage extinction."
